From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:16:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 133/151] Find: match count and all matches highlighted

The find bar shows how many matches the query has ("17 matches"), which
one the last Find next or previous selected ("3 of 17"), "No results",
or "Invalid pattern" with the field in its error state. The count stops
at 10,000 ("10,000+"). It scans each line with the find regex, as Find
next does, and only once typing pauses: 150 ms after a key in the find
field, 300 ms after one in the text (the status bar's counted
generation), so a large file costs one scan per pause, not per key.

While the find bar is open, the matches in the visible rows are tinted
in the accent colour behind the selection. Only the visible lines are
searched when drawing; a line over 64 KiB only around its visible part.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

